From: Kostiantyn Andriiuk <konstantin@andriyuk.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 12:05:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fmscan: add fast scan timing for Vince service indication

The Xiaomi Vince driver exposes a stable binary service indication (zero or
0xffff), not an analogue RSSI value. Use a short settle interval and three
samples so a 100 kHz EU-band scan completes in roughly 45 seconds. Explicitly
unmute during the silent scan and mute before closing the final radio handle.

This is a device integration patch, not a generic fmtools default proposal.
---
 fmscan.c | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fmscan.c b/fmscan.c
index 699038a..166f939 100644
--- a/fmscan.c
+++ b/fmscan.c
@@ -28,9 +28,9 @@
 
 #include "fmlib.h"
 
-#define TRIES		25		/* get 25 samples                 */
-#define LOCKTIME	400000		/* wait 400ms for card to lock on */
-#define SAMPLEDELAY	15000		/* wait 15ms between samples      */
+#define TRIES		3		/* Vince reports binary service   */
+#define LOCKTIME	180000		/* allow firmware tune to settle  */
+#define SAMPLEDELAY	10000		/* reject a transient indication  */
 
 static void
 usage(void)
@@ -111,4 +111,5 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
         tuner_open(&tuner, device, index);
+        tuner_set_mute(&tuner, false);
 
         if (!override) {
                 double min = tuner_get_min_freq(&tuner) / 16000.0;
@@ -172,6 +173,7 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
                                mhz, perc * 100.0);
 	}
 
+        tuner_set_mute(&tuner, true);
         tuner_close(&tuner);
 	return 0;
 }
